abstract: >-
  Python library for market regime detection with Gaussian hidden Markov models, built for
  out-of-sample research. The model is re-estimated on a rolling window (walk-forward), and
  regimes are inferred with the causal forward filter only, so the probabilities of a day use
  data up to that day; invariance tests check that future data never changes past
  probabilities. States are sorted by variance so that labels stay consistent across windows,
  and the number of states can be chosen per window with AIC or BIC. A whipsaw filter reduces
  regime flips at the price of later detection. The evidence in the repository is on synthetic
  data with known states: it is a research library, not a trading strategy or investment
  advice. Import name hmm_regime, PyPI package hmm-regime.
keywords:
  - hidden markov model
  - regime detection
  - walk-forward
  - volatility
  - quantitative finance
